{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    triples_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are three distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    # Sort the list to efficiently use the two-pointer technique.\n    # This approach finds distinct value combinations which correspond to distinct indices\n    # in the original list after sorting.\n    nums = sorted(l)\n\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        # Initialize two pointers, one at the element after current and one at the end.\n        left = i + 1\n        right = n - 1\n        target = -nums[i]\n\n        while left < right:\n            current_sum = nums[left] + nums[right]\n            if current_sum == target:\n                return True  # Found a triplet that sums to zero\n            elif current_sum < target:\n                left += 1  # Need a larger sum, move left pointer right\n            else:\n                right -= 1 # Need a smaller sum, move right pointer left\n\n    return False  # No such triplet found"}
