{"task_id": "HumanEval/95", "solution": "def check_dict_case(dict):\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if all dictionary keys are either all-lowercase strings or all-uppercase strings.\n    Returns False if the dictionary is empty or contains non-string keys or mixed-case string keys.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not dict:\n        return False\n\n    string_keys = []\n    for key in dict.keys():\n        if isinstance(key, str):\n            string_keys.append(key)\n        else:\n            # If any key is not a string, return False as per problem examples.\n            return False\n\n    # At this point, all keys are guaranteed to be strings.\n    # Check if all keys are lowercase.\n    if all(key.islower() for key in string_keys):\n        return True\n    \n    # Check if all keys are uppercase.\n    if all(key.isupper() for key in string_keys):\n        return True\n    \n    # If neither all lowercase nor all uppercase, keys are mixed case.\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/96", "solution": "def count_up_to(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns an array of prime numbers strictly less than n using the Sieve of Eratosthenes.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return []\n\n    # Initialize a boolean array 'sieve' where sieve[i] is true if i is prime.\n    # We use bytearray for memory efficiency with boolean-like values (0 or 1).\n    sieve = bytearray(b'\\x01') * n\n    sieve[0:2] = b'\\x00\\x00'  # 0 and 1 are not prime\n\n    # Iterate from 2 up to sqrt(n).\n    # Any composite number n must have a prime factor less than or equal to sqrt(n).\n    for p in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        # If sieve[p] is still 1 (true), then p is a prime\n        if sieve[p]:\n            # Mark all multiples of p (starting from p*p) as not prime.\n            # Numbers less than p*p that are multiples of p would have already been marked\n            # by smaller prime factors.\n            step = p\n            start = p * p\n            sieve[start:n:step] = b'\\x00' * ((n - 1 - start) // step + 1)\n\n    # Collect all numbers i for which sieve[i] is true.\n    return [i for i, is_prime in enumerate(sieve) if is_prime]"}
